, the record on the middle value of the county&rsquo;s 7 grids runs from 1951 to 2025, and January to February came in under 90% of normal in 35 of those 75 years, more than any other pair. In 2025 the middle of the grids got 47% of normal in November to December and 128% in April to May. This year so far, March to April 2026 came in at 44% on the middle of the grids. Grid 18485 had its driest year in 2007 at 56% of normal.</p>"}
